# Drafted by Gemini (R17 hook), edited.

~ amos_start
Narrator: A mud-booted farmer worries a folded sheet of cream paper between his thumbs, smelling of wet wool and turnip earth.
amos_dority [weary]: Beg pardon, strangers. My cousin Catherine went west to that hospital on the lake for her bad arm, and now this letter comes back in a hand that ain't hers.
* Read the letter. -> amos_letter
* Who is Catherine? -> amos_who
* We will find her. -> amos_accept
* Not now. -> amos_later

~ amos_letter
Narrator: The ink is violet and clerk-neat, without a single blot. It promises that the Matron has healed her, given her purpose, and that she will never come home because all is well.
amos_dority [angry]: Catherine writes like a hen scratching in gravel, and she never used a word like purpose in her life. Somebody else wrote that for her.
-> amos_start

~ amos_who
amos_dority [sad]: Hardest worker on the south acres, till the threshing drum caught her left arm six harvests back. Bone never set right, and she wasn't shy about cursing the ache.
-> amos_start

~ amos_accept
set amos_asked
give mr_letter
quest amos_cousin asked
if not flag.mr_hook_open
set mr_hook_open
give mr_pamphlet
quest all_is_well the_letter
cutscene mr_all_is_well
cutscene mr_all_is_well_2
cutscene end
if not quest.all_is_well >= to_moonsong
quest all_is_well to_moonsong
endif
endif
amos_dority [neutral]: Take this handbill she left behind, and the letter too. It's three nights west down a boggy road to Moonsong Lake, and the paper shows the isle.
-> END

~ amos_later
amos_dority [weary]: Don't leave it too long, I beg you. Blood's blood, and I know when my kin's in trouble.
-> END

~ morgan_pamphlet
Narrator: Between bundles of dried chamomile in the apothecary drawer lies a stiff violet handbill, creased as if opened a hundred times.
morgan [weary]: Oh, that old thing for Memory's Rest. I kept meaning to take the boat out there when my head felt so hollow, only I... well, I never went, and I can't quite recall why.
* Ask what the place is. -> morgan_what
* [if flag.renathyr_journal] I read the Crimson Abbot's journal: his wife fled to the Isle of Mourn. -> morgan_renathyr
* Take the pamphlet. -> morgan_take
* Leave it. -> END

~ morgan_what
morgan [neutral]: A sanatorium out on the lake, run by a very gentle matron, or so the print says. They promise quiet rooms, no more bodily pain, and a clean slate where the bad thoughts were.
-> morgan_pamphlet

~ morgan_renathyr
morgan [afraid]: Let me see the back leaf... yes, founded by a lady widowed of a blessed knight, out on the Isle of Mourn. If the Abbot's wife sought dark waters, that island is the very place.
-> morgan_pamphlet

~ morgan_take
set mr_hook_open
give mr_pamphlet
quest all_is_well the_letter
if not quest.all_is_well >= to_moonsong
quest all_is_well to_moonsong
endif
cutscene mr_all_is_well
cutscene mr_all_is_well_2
cutscene end
morgan [sad]: Keep it, please, before I talk myself into packing a bag. If you do cross the water, and anyone in those halls seems to know my name... tell me when you come back.
-> END
